  "guardImplications": [
    "runtime_scope_allowed requires matching runtime/tenant/entity/branch, active branch, enabled scope, issued_at<=statement_timestamp and expires_at>statement_timestamp.",
    "runtime_worker_required requires worker authority and at least one allowed runtime scope. Edge control calls it before checking its separate enabled/unexpired Edge authority.",
    "edge_schedule_tick on expired authority OR invalid runtime scope unschedules only recorded own jobs with exact reviewed names and disables the Edge authority.",
    "The three API RPC ACLs permit postgres/service_role; four internal functions permit postgres only. All seven captured bodies exactly match local migration bodies, are security definer and set empty search_path.",
    "Catalogue grants and an unsigned403 do not establish actual deployed service credential role/validity. Existing trial through October20 does not bypass worker scope expiry."
  ],
